/applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIROSE MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KATSUO SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA SHOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA JUN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIROSE, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KATSUO, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAKAMURA, SHOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIKAWA, JUN</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>It is judged whether or not AV (Audio Visual) data in each cluster defined by logically dividing a recording medium can be erased on the basis of a free space bite map having the number of references which is the number of files referring to AV data recorded in the clusters.  Therefore, clusters where the number of references is zero are opened as free areas.  Thus, file management is facilitated and the recording medium is efficiently used.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur la question de savoir si les données AV (audiovisuelles) dans chaque fragment défini par la division logique d'un support d'enregistrement peuvent être effacées sur la base d'une carte à multiplets à espace libre ayant un nombre de références égal au nombre de fichiers se référant aux données AV enregistrées dans les fragments. Par conséquent, les fragments où le nombre de références est nul sont ouverts comme des zones disponibles. La gestion de fichiers est ainsi facilitée et le support d'enregistrement est utilisé de manière efficace.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>